                                    -1-
*****************************************************************************
                           Introduction to ADF-DM
*****************************************************************************

Who Am I?
---------

I`m a 20 year old programmer who lives in Northern Ireland, and am currently
working at a software house and am working my way to become a chief software
engineer. I`ve been with the amiga since the age of 13, with the Batman A500
pack, and from this to the A1200 where I did lots of assembly programming
and demo coding. I have about zero free hours a week to work on my personal
projects, so you may guess that ADF-DM was worked on quite hard. Anyway,
enjoy the program and any comments would be thankfully received..

Amiga Disk File Manager
-----------------------

This came from an my own idea, plus a past project for a person called
Dallas. ADF-ZAP a ADF specific hex-editor was developed to allow me to
view a ADF like DiskX would. With this I encluded a `Go To Start Of File`,
this required me reading the ADF and find data inside it, ADF-ZAP make this
easy as I could view any blocks. ADF-DM is a large extension of this, where
it can work with ALL the different data blocks that a AmigaDOS has, it
could read and create the blocks as needed. The program was designed to be
user friendly where you could drap`n`drop files between DOS and the ADF
files. ADF-DM can do more than just copy files from one format to another,
it can test the ADF to see if its compatible and further do a `Disc Doctor`
test on it, though repairing will be done using a future program called
`ADF Doctor` (funny enough!).

Comments, Bugs or Suggestions
-----------------------------

Comments: are very welcome, even if you just say `Downloaded your program
and thought it was good/OK/Shite`, the more feedback the better.

This Version
------------

V1.5c is the first hardfile supporting version of ADF-DM. 




















                                    -2-
*****************************************************************************
                             ADF-DM Interface
*****************************************************************************

First Impressions
-----------------

ADF-DM was designed to keep most windows users `at-home` with the file manager
style program. It includes the drap and drop interface, the copying progress
bar and other `File Manager` styles.

The Main Layout
---------------

The screen is divided into 5 parts. The two main parts which you will use
the most are the ADF directory/file section and the DOS directory/file
secton. When you open an ADF file, its directories and files appear in the
left boxes, when accessing DOS files they appear in the right list boxes.
The third item is the menu, where you can access other `advanced` options,
which can do anything from create a new formatted ADF disk file to test
the current ADF file open. The status bar at the bottom (which can be turned
on or off) displays, what is going on and if any errors have occured, and
finally the tool bar.

The Tool Bar
------------

The tool bar is a newer addition to ADF-DM, allowing you to directly
open/close, format, etc. ADF files without having to touch the menu. The
toolbar's icons and there functions are described below, from left to right.

Open ADF - The first icon opens an ADF, exactly the same as a normal menu
           open.
Close ADF - Close an ADF, because ADF is fully user friendly, you don`t have
            to close and existing ADF before you need to open another one.
            Just use the Open ADF Button, or menu item!

New ADF - This brings up the new adf window, where you can create new DOS
          formatted ADF's for use with UAE and ADF-DM.

New Folder - The four button allows you to create a ADF directory. From here
             you will be presented with a window to select a directory name
             and where you would the dir put.

Normal Test - Use this to do a normal test on the ADF, this will make sure
              the ADF is OK for ADF-DM to read, and that the file's main
              information bits are correct.

Comprehensive Test - Like Normal test, except it does deep testing making
                     sure all bits of every file are correct.

Status Bar Toggle - You can select whether you want to view the status bar
                    from here. This button will also toggle the menu items
                    `tick`.

Find File - This will allow you to find a file in the current ADF.

Find Folder - Similar to find file, except for folders.

Launch ADF-ZAP - This will directly launch ADF-ZAP V1.0e, as supplied

Prefs - Shows the preference window.

Launch Help - Will show this file :)


The Status Bar
--------------

The status bar will give you current information as well as some information
about icons. Its divided into 4 sections..

The first shows how many files are selected in the current ADF, next is
a info box which shows you whats happening (or what an icon does), the
third tells you the size of the ADF, and finally the four box shows you
if its a new or old ADF (FFS - New, OFS - Older)


Pop-Up Menus
------------

The pop-ups menus (Accessed by right-clicking on the ADF or DOS Windows)
gives you easy and fast access to functions like `Delete File`,`Rename File`
or `View File!`










                                    -3-
*****************************************************************************
                          Drapping and dropping
*****************************************************************************


General D`n`D
-------------

Generally Drapping and Dropping is preformed exactly the same as any other
window-based program. You move the pointer over the file you wish to drag,
and hold down the left mouse button on it. Now, start drapping after you
mouse has moved a few pixels (about 1 millimeter on screen), it will change
to a picture of a file - The dragging process has started. Dropping is just
a matter of lifting the file over to the opposite box and letting go of the
left mouse.

Disk Manager D`n`D
------------------

With ADF-DM you can only drag files and not directories. ADF-DM will not
allow you to do any `illegal` drag`n`dropping, so you don`t have to worry
about this.

Multiple D`n`D
--------------

ADF-DM from V1.41 onward supports dragging more than one file at one time.
This is simple, just hold down shift to select more than one file by running
down the list (while holding the left mouse button), when you have finished
simply move the mouse pointer over the last entry and the mouse pointer will
change to a drag pointer, and this must be placed into the opposite directory.
ADF-DM supports extended multiple selection on the lists.

Known Bugs
----------

There is only one known bug with drag`n`dropping and this is more a problem
with Window's and not ADF-DM. When running some Microsoft program's (such
as Word or Excel) you may file that switching between programs and ADF-DM
will disable the drag`n`dropping and you must close and re-open ADF-DM.
This happens will all external drag`n`dropping programs! Someday, microsoft
will start how to learn how to program a good OS.












                                    -4-
*****************************************************************************
                             Opening a ADF file        
*****************************************************************************


Selecting Your File
-------------------

To open your AmigaDOS ADF file, move your pointer up to the menu and select
the main `File` menu. A sub-menu will appear, with a number of options below
it. Select `Open ADF File` and a file requester dialog box will open. You
can also select the first toolbar button, to get the same file requester.From
here, locate your ADF file and click `Open`.

Note : If you have already opened an ADF file don`t worry about closing it
first, ADF-DM will do this automatically when you select `Open ADF File`.

What happens next
-----------------

ADF-DM needs to know what files and directories there are on disk. So at
this point will will look for them. After it has retreived all the files
(including ones in sub-dirs), it will then read in what free space there
is on disk.

Next Step
---------

When ADF-DM has finished processing the ADF it will display the files
and directories in the left two windows.

HARD FILE Support
-----------------

ADF Disk Manager supports hard file upto 16.5Mb in size (which is large
enough for most users). Users should note that due to the larger data
structures for a hard file, some operations (such as bitmap reading/writing)
may take a little longer! 










                                    -5-
*****************************************************************************
                           Moving around ADF/DOS
*****************************************************************************

Moving around DOS
-----------------

Moving around DOS is similar to file manager, except that files and dirs are
keep seperate. The top right box contains directories and double-clicking on
one will show you its contents.

Moving around ADF
-----------------

Is similar to DOS except that you have two extra items at the top of the
ADF directory list. The `.` brings you up a sub-directory while the `..`
brings you back to the main root directory.












                                    -6-
*****************************************************************************
                              Your First Copy
*****************************************************************************

Open an ADF file
----------------

Open an ADF file, preparably a empty formatted one (See below). Now find an
amiga file you want to put on the ADF file, by moving through the DOS boxes
until it appears in the DOS file list. Now, pick up and drag the file onto
the where the files in the ADF appear, and the copy program will commence.

Whats Happening
---------------

ADF-DM is looking now for free space to put your file, it will split you
file across the disk if there is not enough continous space. When ADF
has found the space, it will copy over the file. The progress bar and the
label will keep you informed about who much has been transfered.

Warning
-------

Do not Reset, Shut-Down, Close ADF-DM or in anyway interrupt this copy
process. Its like a real amiga, you interrupt the copying and it might well
invalid the file, and possible corrupt your ADF!












                                    -7-
*****************************************************************************
                               Testing An ADF 
*****************************************************************************

How To Test An AmigaDOS ADF
---------------------------

ADF-DM comes with 3 test to see if your AmigaDOS ADF is OK. Each test is more
advanced that the last one, and will take longer.

Light Test
----------

The light test will allow you to see if an ADF is compatable with ADF-DM, this
checks its AmigaDOS headers and see's if it can spot any obvious problems.
Most Demos/Games will have about 5 errors, if you get this many you will not
be able to run the Normal Or Comprehensive Test (These will automatically
run the Light Test first).

Normal Test
-----------

This will further test the disk and each file on the disk. It will run
through each file making sure that its is valid and can be read (Only headers
not the actual data).

Comprehensive Test
------------------

In addition to the Normal Test, every data block belonging to a file is
tested and evaluated. It any errors are found, they will be reported to
yourself.

Aborting A Test
---------------

To abort a test, simply click the abort button or press return. This will
stop ADF and prompt you with a `Are You Sure` box. NO Damage to your ADF
will result in you selecting Yes Or No, as ADF-DM is only read data not
writting.

At the end of a Test
--------------------

At the end of a test you can select to save a report. This report is saved
on your main C drive, the exact path is given to you by the program.

Help Me To Help You
-------------------

If you get an AmigaDOS ADF file which behaves funny, then please do a
comprehensive test and save a report. Then please e-mail me a ZIP of your
ADF file and report, this will allow me to see (and maybe fix) your ADF.












                                    -8-
*****************************************************************************
                               Analysing ADF's
*****************************************************************************


Analysing
-----------

ADF-DM comes complete with a analysing tool to report different information
about the ADF. You can use these for example to see how much space you have
free.

Bootblock Analysing
-------------------

This will report 3 facts about the boot block which are most important, the
DOS Version, the CheckSum (and if its correct), and the root block position.
NOTE: The root block position should be 880, the amiga supports `flooting`
root blocks (Ie. they don`t have to be at 880), but as 99.99% of AmigaDOS
disks contain it here, I have set this in the code and this will report if
the root block is invalid (and thus inusuable)..

ADF Analysing
-------------

This reports details on the ADF itself, this includes block free, used, bad
and also the disk space free. Users should note that this space free is not
an estimate (like AmigaDOS gives) but a true value. If its says 100K free,
AmigaDOS might say 99K or even 98K free. This is because AmigaDOS estimate
that a file off 100K needs 1K or 2K overhead, and so brings this down.













                                    -9-
*****************************************************************************
                              Renaming your ADF
*****************************************************************************

Renaming
--------

Before you start thinking, why not just go to MS-DOS and use the rename
command to do this? Stop. This doesn`t rename the ADF's MS-DOS name, but
the name that AmigaDOS will see and use. This name is stored internally
and is usually set when you first format the ADF or if you are in workbench
and select the disk icon and rename.

Simple!
-------

Just open your ADF, go to the `Amiga Disk File` menu and select from the
sub-menu `Rename ADF (Root)`. A small window will appear with the existing
name and the a space for you to provide your new name.
When you have entered the new name, select `Rename` .The ADF will be renamed,
and you will be returned to the main ADF-DM window. If you don`t want to
rename the file, simply click `Cancel` or close the window.








                                    -10-
*****************************************************************************
                         Creating Formatted ADF's
*****************************************************************************

ADF-DM comes with the facility to created formatted or unformatted ADF disk
files. The main advantage being that you do not need to go to DOS and use
MakeDisk to create your ADF, and then let UAE (slowly) format your ADF file.
ADF-DM will create AND format you ADF in 2 seconds (P133 32Mb).

Opening The Creation Window
---------------------------

Move to the `New` main menu, and move down to the `New Image` sub menu.
Currently only one option exists here, and thats for a `ADF (Formatted)`.
Select this, and a window appears, where you can select the type of format,
along with the ADF's name and a few other details..

General Info About Creation
---------------------------

Creation requires only one main item, and thats what you want to call the
ADF file when its created. This is defaulted to `C:\AMIGA\CREATED.ADF`, this
is changable *BUT* will be defaulted to everything you close and re-open the
window.

Options
-------

Options for creation includes..

Disk Name : You can change the disk name (upto 28 characters) and this can
            include spaces and most alphanumber characters. ADF-DM will place
            onto the ADF whatever name you want, even if AmigaDOS will not
            allow you to (IE. AmigaDOS doesn`t allow colon's but ADF-DM
            does - though I don`t recommend :-)

Dos Path : Where you want to place the file when its created. This can be
           anywhere on any drive. Just remember that ADF-DM does not check
           for free space, so if you doesn`t have enough space.. Except a
           UAE [ Unrecoverable Application Error! ;-( ]

Quick Format : NOT ENABLED - When enabled quick format will not format each
               track similar to DOS. It will just create a file with crap in
               it (like MakeDisk). When not running in Quick Mode formatting
               can take much longer - This is due for inclusion in later
               versions, but it makes little sense to use it.

Inc. DOS : (Include DOS) This will allow you to actually `Format` Or
           `Initailise` the ADF so that UAE can see it. This will create and
           format the ADF with the name and type supplied.

DOS Type : A combo is used to select whether you want FFS or OFS. They both
           have advantages over each other. FFS is faster, and allow more
           files to be put on a disk. OFS is more secure and will find errors
           better, its up to you. (Personally, FFS is best as its keeps UAE's
           speed up)

Creating Your ADF
-----------------

Once you have your entered your settings, its time to actually create your
ADF. ADF-DM will process to create and then (if enabled) format and prepare
you ADF for use. Creation takes less than a second, and formatting not much
longer (P133 32Mb). If the file exists, or there is a problem you will be
informed, and you should take action to correct this!

Please Note
-----------

ADF files created by ADF-DM are one byte longer than normal ADF's. Don`t
worry this is a problem with the language user to create ADF-DM, and UAE
doesn`t worry in the slightest.











                                    -11-
*****************************************************************************
                         Creating New Directories..
*****************************************************************************

Creating New Directories
------------------------

To create sub-directories in DOS or ADF files is easy. Simply select from
the `New` menu, `New Folder` and then what sort of folder a DOS one, or a
folder in a ADF file.

General Usage
-------------

You will then be presented with a window where you enter the directory name
and where you would like the directory placed. This can be either the main
root or the current sub-directory. Once you have enter the details and
selected the destination, click `Make Dir` to create the directory..

DOS directories
---------------

Are created the same as window or dos would create the directory. The dir
does not appear instantly, you must reselect the dir (or review it) by
clicking (double-clicking) on the parent directory.

ADF directories
---------------

ADF directories take a little longer to generate, but is about 25 times
fast than Workbench's MakeDir command (running via UAE). It will also update
the bitmap so that no other files will overwrite the directories. ADF Dirs
appear automatically when created.










                                    -12-
*****************************************************************************
                              Viewing Settings
*****************************************************************************

Settings
--------

Under the View menu, there are a number of options available to you. These
change the way ADF-DM looks and acts, most of them are implemented and so
this section needs to be expanded.

Status Bar
----------

The status bar shows the current process in a scroll type manar, its also
shows errors. To disable the status bar, simply move the pointer over it
and leave go, the bar will disappear and the lists will resize to take up
its space. To show it again, simply repeat the process.

Auto Refresh
------------

Auto refresh works the same as the status bar, in the sense of how to hide
or show it. The function itself, doesn`t. The program will auto-refresh
the ADF window not matter what is selected here, so you can leave it alone.

F.A.T
-----

The File Allocation Table (What MS-DOS calls it) or Block Bitmap (What
AmigaDOS calls it), is a list of free blocks. This view option allows you to
see whats in the F.A.T. - Red blocks are used, and green are free. The FAT
window also displays block and bytes free on your ADF.

NOTE: When you format an ADF and do this, there are always 3 blocks used,
these hold the start off the operating system and file system so don`t worry.


















                                    -13-
*****************************************************************************
                         Finding Files Or Folders
*****************************************************************************

Finding Files Or Folders
------------------------

Is done, via the tools menu. From there selected the sub-menu `Find` and
then select whether its a file or folder you want to file. A window will
appear with a combo box, containing all files or folders. Select a file
or folder from that list and its full path will appear below in the label.

Type Your Own Searches
----------------------

With newer versions you can type your file name directly into the combo and
ADF-DM will look up the location of the file/folder when you press return.
This is not case-sensitive.




















                                    -14-
*****************************************************************************
 *NEW*                           Preferences                           *NEW*
*****************************************************************************

Preferences
-----------

Preferences is a new part of amiga disk file manager and now you`ll find its
even more configurable.

Preferences window
------------------

The main preferences window is divided into 3 sections. The left frame holds
the currently displayed `sub-preference`. The second section is where you
can gain access (via button) to different sub-preferences such as the toolbar,
window settings, etc.. The third section is the save and applying section.


REGISTER PREFS
**************

Versiof V1.45 and above of ADF-DM are now shareware. This means that you get
the full program, free of charge, but are required to pay a small amount for
the program. This prefs holds the current registration details and is where
you will go if you require technical support, help or version updates. Using
your user name and registration number you can log-onto the ADF-Suite
homepage and request/receive information on any part of ADF-Suite. This
section tells you how to register


CONVERTER PREFS
***************

The converter for most of ADF-DM functions is fast enough to run on a P75 and
above. Lower end machines will require the disabling of task switching during
read/write or bitmap operations.
If you think ADF-DM is too slow converting, try click these buttons and then
applying the settings. ADF-DM will now not allow Window's to interrupt it
when converting, read or writing to the ADF or using the ADF's bitmap.

NOTES: This disables task switching temporarly. P90 and above will probably
notice no difference.

WARNINGS: This will prevent other tasks (including communication programs)
from getting access to the system. If you are using a LAN you may lose packets
if on the InterNet you will again lose packets. You have been warned..


TOOL BAR PREFS
**************

The tool bar is now fully configurable. You can change the tool bar to what
ever you want, and include or remove what buttons you don`t want.

Start afresh!
-------------

Click on the `< X` button to clear the existing tool box. This will allow
you to build your new tool bar from scratch.

Adding buttons
--------------

Click on the right list of available buttons, and then click on the `<` button
to put the button on the tool bar. The new button will go in after the current
selection in the current list.

Removing buttons
----------------

Simply click on the button you want to remove (the left list), and then
click on the `>` icon. It will be removed and placed in the available list.

Spacing
-------

There is no limit to the amount of spacing you can put between to icons as
long as the number of icons in the whole toolbar is less than or equal to
20. The `Space` button always exists in the available list.

Auto Update Main Form
---------------------

This check box beneath the main lists is used to update the tool bar as soon
as something is added or deleted. This is handly to see your new tool bar
without having to click on apply.

Apply Button
------------

If you chose not to auto apply your toolbar, then use this button to make
your new tool bar.

Reset To Defaults
-----------------

Screw up with the tool bar? This is automatically rebuild the toolbar using
the internal default values. This is handy if you want to make only mild
changes or get fed up!


WINDOW PREFS
************

The window preferences tell ADF-DM how to resize and control the DOS and
ADF windows. There are 3 options here, to control the autoresizing and
status bar.

Auto Resize DOS/ADF windows within main window
----------------------------------------------

This option will allow you to toggle whether ADF-DM will auto-resize the
DOS and ADF window inside the main ADF-DM window. The DOS/ADF windows take
up half of the space each and are automatically reposition and scaled when
you change the size of the main window. Toggling this off means that the
DOS/ADF windows will stay the same size, no matter what happens to the main
window.

Auto Resize dir/file lists within the sub-windows
-------------------------------------------------

This toggles whether the lists inside each of the DOS and ADF files are
auto-resized when the size of the DOS/ADF window changes. There will be
few people who will set this to off :-)

Display StatusBar on startup
----------------------------

Toggles whether the startbar is on/off when the program is started. By
default the statusbar is on, but you can take it off here.


FILE LOCATIONS
**************

This is used to set a few default places for ADF-DM to look for ADF's and
important files.

Default Location Of ADF's
-------------------------

This stores the default location of ADF's. My personal preferences is C:\AMIGA
but this can be anything you want it to be! When you first open the File
Dialog this directly is the current one.

ADF-Zap EXE Location
--------------------

This is ignored, and not implemented.

Generated Reports Path
----------------------

This is ignored, and not implemented

Pattern used in DOS File List
-----------------------------

If you want a certain type of file to be displayed in the DOS File List then
select it here. The default is *.* (all files), but for example if you just
want text files enter *.TXT or ADF files *.ADF.


APPLY AND SAVING YOUR SETTINGS
******************************

Save and apply button
---------------------




                                    -15-
*****************************************************************************
                           Tools For Your ADF..
*****************************************************************************

Loading ADF-ZAP Directly from ADF-DM
------------------------------------

This feature is used to run ADF-ZAP directly from ADF-DM without first
having to close it down. This feature is accessed from the `Tools` menu and
requires that you have ran the setup program and its has completed correctly,
and ADF-ZAP is in the correct directory.

Deleted File Recovery
---------------------

A very handy feature if you delete files by mistake! It will search your
ADF's to find out if there are any deleted files on it, if there are any
found you can un-delete them, copy them to dos or have a look at them!

Select from the `Tools` menu, `File Recovery`. This will bring up the file
recovery menu and start ADF-DM reading the disk. This process is very fast,
it is many times faster than other Amiga Products and will track down files
alot harder! Once the process has finished, you will see your files along
with their condition (Sorry, not implemented yet!).

UnDelete File - This will try and re-instate the link between the file and
                its parent directory. Be careful! Files have to links, a
                forward and backward link. The backward says who its parent
                is (and if the directories doesn`t exist, it won`t undelete)
                and a forward link (to the next file in the chain). If the
                forward link points to a file thats deleted, or somewhere
                else you could be in for fun. BUT remember if you have just
                deleted a file, undeleting will be safe!
Copy To Dos - Is used to copy a file to dos, if undelete doesn`t work. This
              sometimes doesn`t work because of the complexity of AmigaDOS,
              and just telling AmigaDOS thats its there does work!
              Files will be copied as they are named directly to the current
              DOS directory.
View Hex/Ascii - This allows you to view the file prior to dumping it out!
                 You can see if the data is still there, and how much
                 damage has been done by new files overwritting it..


Track Dumping
-------------

This allows you to dump tracks directly from an ADF to anywhere on the your
PC's hard disk. Handy for people wanting to get text/graphics/code from
trackloading ADF's!

Select the start and end tracks, enter the file name (including path) and
then select `dump`. ADF-DM automatically assigns a file name, as being
the ADF's name + `.DMP`... Its up to you to change this..

If anyone needs to feature of Block output (There are 22 blocks in a track)
then please let me know..








                                    -16-
*****************************************************************************
                     Known Bugs (fixes) and Workarounds
*****************************************************************************

ADF-DM - Known Bugs
-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

Bug> During Comprehensive Tests on OFS files sometimes the filename is not
     displayed during the block test.

ADF-DM - Bug Fixes!    (Version indicates where the bug came from..)
-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

Bug> (V1.1)  File over 20 characters would appear (truncated) and would cause
             ADF-DM to crash if converter..
Bug> (V1.1a) File creation routine very bugy, and was removed.
Bug> (V1.0)  The ADF analysis returned incorrect results with block free/used
Bug> (V1.0)  When showing external programs (Help, ADF-ZAP) they were run in
             minimised form.
Bug> (V1.0)  ADF-DM will not accept amiga files with non-standard characters
Bug> (V1.41) When a different directory was chosen to install ADF-DM, the
             ZAP and HELP launched still looked in a set place.
Bug> (V1.41) The boot file was not copied to the correct dir when installing
             ADFSuite in a non-standard dir.
Bug> (V1.41) Delete an ADF file would not work right for two reasons. The
             first is that it would not redo the checksum on the FHB and it
             would not free up the space taken by the file :(
Bug> (V1.45) Rename Root, didn`t change the name of the ADF at run-time.


