                                    -17-
*****************************************************************************
                            Terms And Reference
*****************************************************************************

ADF-DM is generally going to be off use to only a few people who have been
working with amiga emulators and require getting external programs and files
directly onto ADF's without using an amiga or going near TransDisk. This
reference section is generally for people who do not know Amiga words or
phrases..

Boot Block - The first 2 blocks on a disk, where the boot strap code lies.
Root Block - The root block is where the main (root) directories starts and
             all files exist (via links) to this dir.
Block      - A 512 byte section of disk, the amiga has 1760 block per disk.
Checksum   - A value used to verify that data in a block is correct and hasn't
             been chanced (or corrupt)

 [If there a word you would like to know what it means then please e-mail me]















